# Behavioral Modeling in Verilog

This directory contains high-level behavioral RTL implementations and corresponding simulation testbenches. Unlike gate-level structural modeling, behavioral modeling describes circuit functionality algorithmically using procedural blocks (`always @(*)`), conditional logic, and behavioral operators (`^`, `&`, `+`).


